# Downloadable files

When the user asks for a file (zip, txt, xml, pdf, image, installer, or any other artifact they should take with them), **that turn is not done until they can download it**.

1. Copy the file to `/opt/cursor/artifacts/<filename>` (Cursor download tray).
2. Commit a copy under repo-root `patches/<filename>` (same pattern as InPmnt-PHP.zip) and push.
3. In the **user-facing reply**, the download must be a **public HTTPS URL** the user can open in a browser. Never `/opt/cursor/artifacts/...` — that path is not web-accessible to them.
   - Zip (this is what they click): `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/devildog5x5/InPmnt/<branch>/patches/<filename>`
   - Same pattern as InPmnt-PHP.zip. Still copy to `/opt/cursor/artifacts/` for the tray, but **do not** put that path in the chat as the download link.
4. If you built more than one file, make **every** one downloadable the same way.
5. Prefer a **versioned** filename (`FamilyShieldPro-1.0.0.zip`) plus a latest alias (`FamilyShieldPro.zip`).
6. Never send `robots.txt`, `sitemap.xml`, or other text as a GitHub raw URL when the user needs a file — the browser shows the data. Put those files **inside the product zip** and give only the zip as the download.
7. Do not give `/opt/cursor/artifacts/` as a download link. It is not a web URL.
